/*
Problem: Maximum Product Difference Between Two Pairs (LC 1913)
Topic: Array / Greedy

--------------------------------------------------

Idea:

We need to maximize:

(max1 × max2) - (min1 × min2)

So we only need:

• The two largest numbers.

• The two smallest numbers.

Find all four values in a single
traversal without sorting.

--------------------------------------------------

Algorithm:

1. Initialize:

   max1, max2

   min1, min2

2. Traverse the array.

3. Update the two largest numbers.

4. Update the two smallest numbers.

5. Compute:

   (max1 × max2)
   -
   (min1 × min2)

6. Return the answer.

--------------------------------------------------

Example:

Input:

[5,6,2,7,4]

Largest:

7, 6

Smallest:

2, 4

Answer:

(7 × 6) - (2 × 4)

= 42 - 8

= 34

--------------------------------------------------

Example:

Input:

[4,2,5,9,7,4,8]

Largest:

9, 8

Smallest:

2, 4

Answer:

72 - 8

= 64

--------------------------------------------------

Why It Works?

To maximize the expression:

(max product) - (min product)

we must choose:

• The two largest values for the
  first product.

• The two smallest values for the
  second product.

A single scan is enough to keep
track of these four numbers.

--------------------------------------------------

Time : O(n)

Single traversal of the array.

Space : O(1)

Only four variables are used.

--------------------------------------------------

Pattern:

Greedy / One Pass Array
*/

class Solution {
public:
    int maxProductDifference(vector<int>& nums) {

        int max1 = 0, max2 = 0;
        int min1 = INT_MAX, min2 = INT_MAX;

        for (int x : nums) {

            // Update two largest numbers
            if (x > max1) {
                max2 = max1;
                max1 = x;
            }
            else if (x > max2) {
                max2 = x;
            }

            // Update two smallest numbers
            if (x < min1) {
                min2 = min1;
                min1 = x;
            }
            else if (x < min2) {
                min2 = x;
            }
        }

        return (max1 * max2) - (min1 * min2);
    }
};
